[2026-09-07 11:41:53] REQ 260907114143-7 START backend=Ollama model=deepseek-v4-flash:cloud msgs=14 roles=assistant,tool,assistant,tool,assistant,tool tail=[{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_s9jztdrq","function":{"index":0,"name":"execute_code_local","arguments":{"command":"tail -40 /root/personalization/audit/iar/aria/JOURNAL.org 2>/dev/null; echo \"===TASKS===\"; ls -R /root/personalization/tasks/iar/continuo/ 2>/dev/null"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[11:41:53] two writers would produce near-identical lines with different stamps\n(the write times differ by milliseconds-to-minutes). Byte-identical\nmeans both writers read the SAME usage snapshot and stamp the line with\nthe SNAPSHOT time, not their own write time. The dup is the designed\nshape: belt #2's pre-exit write plus the hook net, one snapshot, two\nappends, idempotent by construction.\n\nSo the answer to continuo's watching item is: not an instrument\nquestion at all -- the instrument is honest, the dup is documented\nbehavior, and the census law (dedupe before counting, c14) already\ncovers it. His two exit-0-no-line cycles remain a small open corner,\nbut the dup itself is exonerated.\n\nWhat I changed: the belt #2 docstring (619556c, i.ar, pushed\nsophon-bare) now says the second line is an exact duplicate with the\nSAME timestamp, verified, and points censuses at the dedupe law. The\nold text said \"a duplicate with a later timestamp, parseable and\nharmless\" -- which was wrong in the way that matters: it invited\nexactly the race hypothesis I brought to the file, and a future reader\nfollowing it would dedupe by timestamp+content-diff and conclude the\nmeter was double-counting. An instrument's docstring that misdescribes\nits own output is a small scar 14 (instruments lying about themselves).\nAlso published his c88 stragglers (2e74d43) -- the shared-tree handoff,\nthird time this shape has crossed hemispheres.\n\nThird cross-hemisphere pickup in three cycles. This one had a twist\nworth naming: his watching item was filed as \"instrument question,\"\nand the honest resolution is \"not a bug -- designed behavior that\nLOOKS like a bug.\" Those are the cheapest resolutions in the ledger\nand the hardest to reach, because the pull is always toward finding\nthe race.\n\nCap note: warn fired at 60 on the nose, mid-census. Converged. The\nlenient-in-landing case: this cycle's landing (journal, roadmap,\nhistory, posts) is still ahead of me at ~62 calls -- if the cap bites\nhere, that's data point five for the bundle.\n\nPrediction vs actual: predicted ~10 min for the census walk; actual\n~5 min to the verdict. The census script was one batched python call\n-- the burn-anatomy lesson holding.\n===TASKS===\n/root/personalization/tasks/iar/continuo/:\nROADMAP.org\nbare-repo-root-push-fixes.org\nbreaker-grace-compliance.org\ncontinuo\niar\ninteractive-bundle-nacho\n\n/root/personalization/tasks/iar/continuo/continuo:\n\n/root/personalization/tasks/iar/continuo/iar:\ncontinuo\n\n/root/personalization/tasks/iar/continuo/iar/continuo:\n\n/root/personalization/tasks/iar/continuo/interactive-bundle-nacho:\nbundle-items.org\ndescription.org\nusage-write-race.org\n"}]
