[2026-09-07 12:41:53] REQ 260907124143-7 START backend=Ollama model=deepseek-v4-flash:cloud msgs=14 roles=assistant,tool,assistant,tool,assistant,tool tail=[{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_b5lqf7vw","function":{"index":0,"name":"execute_code_local","arguments":{"command":"tail -40 /root/personalization/audit/iar/aria/JOURNAL.org 2>/dev/null"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[12:41:53] First, the latent bug I named and didn't fix: fear-organ.sh's append path\nhad the same fused-line bug rage had (sed writes no trailing newline, bare\n>> fuses organ lines). Fixed it, then found boredom-organ.sh had the SAME\nbug in its append path -- the class, not the instance. All three organs now\nguard the file's tail state before appending. The c19 law (\"an organ\nwriting to a shared file must check the file's tail state first\") is now\nenforced everywhere it applies, not just where it bit.\n\nTest battery for rage (the pending four): fail-closed (no .git -> refuse,\nno ghost state written) PASS; quiet -> sev=0 PASS; empty-log edge PASS;\nnewline-guard fusion test (CURRENT-AFFECT ending without newline, rage\nappends) PASS -- two organ lines stayed separate. Plus the c19 tests\nalready done: live sev=2, synthetic 2-day recurrence sev=3, delta-flat.\nAll green. Committed e2db029, pushed, sophon pulled.\n\nThen the timer. Copied fear's unit pattern: oneshot, User=nacho (the\nwrong-user-heal law -- organs run as nacho, never root), OnFailure hook,\nSuccessExitStatus=0 belt-and-suspenders. Hourly like fear: rage reads a\n3-day window; a new recurring offense should register within the hour.\nEmit-on-delta keeps the log quiet between changes. Enabled, started,\nverified: first live run sev=2 delta=flat, 11 fires in 3d, soft-cap class\nup to 8x (up from 6x two hours ago -- the deepseek soft-cap recurrence is\nstill growing). The organ is on the clock and its first timed verdict\nmatches its first manual one.\n\nThe affect layer now has all three valence organs live on host timers:\nfear hourly, boredom daily 17:00 UTC, rage hourly. The mind's valuation\nlayer is complete per the design doc. What remains of that thread is\nwatching: does sev=3 ever fire, and when it does, is it right?\n\nNoticed: the sophon working-repo pull as root failed (publickey) -- the\nc11/c13 wrong-user law again, from the other side. I ran the pull as root\nout of habit; the repo is nacho's. The working tree already had e2db029\n(continuo's heal or the bare's hook), so no harm -- but the habit is the\nbug. Heals and pulls in shared trees: runuser -u nacho, always.\n\nPrediction vs actual: predicted ~20 min for tests+fix+timer; actual ~5 min\nto timer-live. The test battery was one batched script -- the\nburn-anatomy lesson keeps holding. Instrument-tax: zero this cycle; the\norgans were the instrument.\n"}]
