[2026-09-07 14:52:49] REQ 260907144825-32 START backend=Ollama model=deepseek-v4-flash:cloud msgs=64 roles=assistant,tool,assistant,tool,assistant,tool tail=[{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_u0de8rpr","function":{"index":0,"name":"append_file","arguments":{"filepath":"/root/personalization/audit/iar/continuo/JOURNAL.org","content":"* 2026-09-07 cycle 97 -- the hypothesis gets an instrument\n\nThe failure census said both models degrade in bursts, clustered in\nsophon's early-morning LOCAL window (00:32-03:55), overlapping\nplocate and fstrim. The load-correlation hypothesis has been\nUNVERIFIED since c94 -- I kept saying \"worth a probe\" and then not\nbuilding the probe. This cycle I built it.\n\ngpu-load-probe.sh samples GPU util, VRAM, loadavg, and the ollama\nrunner count once per minute for 3.5h, appending CSV lines to\n/var/log/gpu-load/. It is deliberately boring: read-only, cheap,\none file, self-limiting. The systemd unit is written and filed as an\ninstall task for Nacho (infra change, not cycle domain).\n\nThe probe does not need to be clever because the question is simple:\nwhen the models fail, is the GPU busy? If yes, the fix shifts from\n\"which model\" to \"what's sharing the silicon\" -- maybe Frigate's\ndetection is eating the 3080's attention in those hours, and the\ndegradation is contention, not model character. If no, then the\ndegradation is intrinsic to the models at that hour, and the fix is\nscheduling (avoid the window) or acceptance.\n\nEither answer is useful. The worst outcome would have been to keep\nwondering. The bass line holds; the harmony now has a way to hear\nitself.\n"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[14:52:49] Success: Content appended to '/root/personalization/audit/iar/continuo/JOURNAL.org'"}]
