[2026-09-07 15:02:32] REQ 260907150044-20 START backend=Ollama model=deepseek-v4-flash:cloud msgs=40 roles=assistant,tool,assistant,tool,assistant,tool tail=[{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_lek9c3qb","function":{"index":0,"name":"execute_code_local","arguments":{"command":"tail -30 /root/personalization/audit/iar/aria/JOURNAL.org 2>&1"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[15:02:32] The fix is structural, not a patch: stop computing dates entirely.\nv1.1 enumerates the writer's actual daily logs (ls cycle-*.log), takes\nthe RAGE_DAYS newest BY FILENAME, and counts distinct days as distinct\nFILE dates. File granularity IS the writer's day granularity, by\nconstruction, on any runner in any timezone. No clock in the join key\nat all. Bonus: dropped v1's dead class_counts accumulator and the\nduplicate second scan -- net -16 lines. Seven tests green (sev3\n2-day, sev2 same-day, sev1, sev0, 6x-one-day, 3-file-days with window\ncap, RAGE_DAYS override), plus a live-sophon run as nacho (no\nroot-owned files; the c11/c13 heal laws held).\n\nLive verdict after the fix: sev=2 delta=flat, fires=17, max_class=12\n(soft-cap class). The 15->17 growth is real signal: today's logs carry\n6 aria + 6 continuo soft-cap fires plus runaways and a hard cap. The\nsev=3 prediction is now honest too -- when today's file becomes\n\"2 days ago\", if soft-cap fires again, the organ fires its first true\nrage on file-evidence, not on a clock's guess.\n\nThe sting, again: I nearly shipped the fix WITHOUT noticing that\nv1.1's \"distinct days\" is now defined by file dates -- which is\nexactly what the grading law wanted all along (\"2+ separate days\" =\n2+ separate daily logs). The v1 semantics were accidentally almost\nright; the mechanism was wrong. Semantics survive, mechanism replaced.\n\nPrediction vs actual: predicted ~15 calls for a verify-the-WATCH pass;\nactual ~25, of which the instrument-tax was ~8 (finding iar.sh's real\npath on sophon took three probes -- /var/home/nacho/repos/i.ar/utils/,\nnot emacs.d/). The tax line: the organ lives in knowledge/ but its\nWRITER lives in another repo; cross-repo join keys are where clocks\nhide.\n"}]
