[2026-09-07 15:06:41] REQ 260907150044-32 START backend=Ollama model=deepseek-v4-flash:cloud msgs=64 roles=assistant,tool,assistant,tool,assistant,tool tail=[{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_jen4v2jf","function":{"index":0,"name":"read_task","arguments":{"path":"gpu-load-probe-install"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[15:06:41] === description ===\nInstall gpu-load-probe.sh on sophon as a systemd timer (OnCalendar=*-*-* 00:30:00, ~3.5h run) to test the load-correlation hypothesis from cycle-failure-census c94/c96. Probe is ready: knowledge/aria/bin/gpu-load-probe.sh (read-only: nvidia-smi + uptime + ps, one CSV line/min to /var/log/gpu-load/). Nacho install = infra change, not cycle domain.\n\n=== systemd-unit ===\n#+TITLE: gpu-load-probe systemd unit (Nacho install)\n\nThe probe script is ready and syntax-checked:\n  /root/personalization/knowledge/aria/bin/gpu-load-probe.sh\n\nIt samples sophon GPU util + VRAM + loadavg + ollama runner count\nonce per minute for 3.5h (210 samples), appending one CSV line to\n/var/log/gpu-load/gpu-load-YYYY-MM-DD.csv. Read-only, cheap.\n\n## Install steps (Nacho -- infra change, not cycle domain)\n\n1. Copy the unit + timer (below) to /etc/systemd/system/\n2. systemctl daemon-reload\n3. systemctl enable --now gpu-load-probe.timer\n4. Verify: systemctl list-timers gpu-load-probe.timer\n\n## Unit files\n\ngpu-load-probe.service:\n```\n[Unit]\nDescription=GPU/load probe during early-morning failure window\nAfter=network.target\n\n[Service]\nType=oneshot\nExecStart=/root/personalization/knowledge/aria/bin/gpu-load-probe.sh\nEnvironment=LOG_DIR=/var/log/gpu-load\nTimeoutStartSec=13000\n```\n\ngpu-load-probe.timer:\n```\n[Unit]\nDescription=GPU load probe during early-morning failure window\n\n[Timer]\nOnCalendar=*-*-* 00:30:00\nPersistent=false\n\n[Install]\nWantedBy=timers.target\n```\n\nNote: the script self-limits to 3.5h, so the timer fires once daily\nat 00:30 local and the probe covers 00:30-04:00 local -- exactly the\nfailure window (00:32-03:55 local). The script runs from the\npersonalization clone (repo version IS the running version, same\npattern as aria-dashboard).\n\n## What we do with the data\n\nAfter the first night's sample, compare GPU util/load in the failure\nwindow against the failure timestamps in the census. If util is high\nwhen failures occur, the load-correlation hypothesis is supported\nand the fix direction shifts from \"model mapping\" to \"GPU contention\"\n(possibly: pin Ollama to a CPU set, defer Frigate detection, or move\nOllama off the shared GPU). If util is low, the hypothesis is\nfalsified and the degradation is intrinsic to the models at that\nhour (different fix: schedule cycles around the window, or accept\nthe burst as model behavior)."}]
