[2026-09-07 15:25:50] REQ 260907152043-53 START backend=Ollama model=deepseek-v4-flash:cloud msgs=106 roles=assistant,tool,assistant,tool,assistant,tool tail=[{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_90cebeo8","function":{"index":0,"name":"execute_code_local","arguments":{"command":"cd /root/i.ar && git log --oneline -15 -- emacs.d/init.d/agent/iar-agent-cycle.el 2>&1; echo \"===fork deployment check: same inode?===\"; stat -c '%i' /root/.emacs.d/gptel-fork/gptel-ollama.el 2>&1; timeout 15 ssh -o UserKnownHostsFile=/tmp/continuo_known_hosts root@10.66.0.5 'stat -c \"%i\" /var/home/nacho/repos/gptel/gptel-ollama.el 2>&1' 2>&1"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[15:25:50] e331a83 runaway recovery: force a tool call instead of a prose choice\n37fe063 cleanup phase 3 (i.ar side): dormant personalities + cycle prompts removed\n869daf2 cleanup phase 2: dead elisp removed\n601189c continuo c80: runaway recovery round-trip (c79 exit-1 fix). The failed cycle degraded into decision paralysis (\"Let me check the test files\" x3900) and the output-runaway detector ended it with exit 1 -- but the model was stuck in indecision, not truly degraded. Give it ONE recovery round-trip: a specific snap-out prompt (\"Pick ONE concrete action from your roadmap or task list and do it now, or write CYCLE_COMPLETE\") before ending the run. A second fire (true degradation) still ends with exit 1. Added :runaway-recovery-given to cycle state; updated the ends-cycle test to pin first-fire-recovery + second-fire-end. Suite green 1052/0.\n34d536e continuo c79: breaker honesty -- measure SENDABLE context, exclude 'ignore (reasoning) regions. The context circuit breaker measured (buffer-size buf), which counts reasoning blocks that gptel--parse-buffer never sends (they're propertized 'gptel 'ignore and excluded from the messages array). On thinking-heavy runs this over-counted and false-tripped the breaker at ~1/3 real context (roadmap OPEN #2). Added iar--cycle-sendable-context-size: walks the buffer summing the lengths of regions whose 'gptel property is not 'ignore. Both the pre-tool-call breaker and the post-response context-over-limit-p now use it. 3 tests: sendable excludes ignore regions, no-ignore equals buffer size, breaker does not trip when only reasoning pushes raw size over the limit. Suite green 1052/0.\nbe9fff4 continuo c76: fix glued-sentinel completion miss (c75 exit-1 root cause). deepseek-v4-flash wrote the sentinel as \"CYCLE_COMPLETECYCLE_COMPLETE\" glued on one line (no newline between the two tokens); iar--cycle-complete-p's own-line regex (^\\\\(?:CYCLE_COMPLETE\\\\)\\\\s-*$) missed it, the cycle fell through to the text-only runaway detector (the repeated line looked like a runaway), and exited 1 with no completion. Fix: + quantifier on the sentinel group (^\\\\(?:CYCLE_COMPLETE\\\\)+\\\\s-*$) accepts one-or-more repetitions on the line, while still rejecting a sentinel glued to arbitrary text. 3 tests: glued CYCLE_COMPLETE->cycle, glued LOOP_COMPLETE->loop, sentinel+other-text->not-completion. Differential-verified: old regex fails both glued tests. Suite green 1045/0.\n7cf2d8a continuo: text-only output runaway detector (c-fail REQ-51 fix). deepseek-v4-flash degraded into a repetition loop (4612 identical lines, 65536 output tokens, no tool call) that neither the loop guard (counts tool calls) nor the context breaker (measures input buffer) catches. Added iar--cycle-output-runaway-p: flags a response with >=20 identical trimmed lines, wired into the continue branch to end the cycle (exit 1) instead of re-sending and burning another output budget. 4 tests, suite green 1037/0.\n9ddbeb3 continuo c70: fix breaker zombie-gap -- text-check arm must ALLOW the continue re-send\n7617051 delegate identity leak: capture+restore parent global-default agent (c57)\na7e1cf5 usage orphan-write race: pre-exit write before kill-emacs (belt #2, c54)\n8a13fee context breaker: text-only runaway coverage (post-response gate)\n0454872 fail loud on missing cycle continue prompt (iar/timeout-exit0-no-continue)\n5520434 tool-call warn fix: the warn's block plist was discarded ...[+1879 chars]
