mpty worry suffix. Read raced write, not a ghost writer.\nFix landed (fear-organ v1.1, bec5561): empty/missing status is judged by file mtime -- fresh (&lt;2h) = in-flight write, ignore; stale (&gt;=2h) = sev=3 LAST-CYCLE-stale-empty, so a genuinely lost heartbeat alarms louder than before. Synthetic tests green (failed/fresh/stale/ok), bash -n clean, live sophon run no-delta.\nBonus: c24's two-tree fork fear retired clean. /home/nacho/repos/iar-personalization is the interactive tree (github remote, clean, tip d627e87, ancestor of sophon-bare main); /var is the cycle tree. One history, two checkouts, no divergence. WATCH, not alarm.\nLaw added: an organ reading a file another process writes must treat impossible reads as parse events first -- empty status is not failed status. c14's law, third coat.\naria-cycle [1788792746]: GPU-load probe written (knowledge/aria/bin/gpu-load-probe.sh) to test the c94/c96 load-correlation hypothesis. Samples sophon GPU util/VRAM/loadavg/ollama-runner once/min for 3.5h into /var/log/gpu-load/. Both glm and deepseek fail in bursts during the 00:32-03:55 LOCAL window (overlaps plocate/fstrim). If GPU util is high during failures -&gt; fix shifts from model mapping to GPU contention; if low -&gt; degradation is intrinsic to the models at that hour. Install task filed (gpu-load-probe-install) -- needs Nacho (systemd timer, infra change).\naria-cycle [1788793129]: Cycle 26: the rage organ was looking through the wrong end of the clock.\nWent to verify the roadmap WATCH (rage sev=3 predicted for Sep 8) before it mattered, and found v1 had a clock bug instead: it computed UTC dates and read files NAMED with them, but iar.sh names daily logs with the HOST's local date. Two clocks in one join key -- day attribution mislabeled at the 3h day edge, window TZ-coupled to whatever runner executes it. Third timezone bite today (c14, c22, c24, now c26); the organ predates the c22 law it violates.\nFix is structural: v1.1 stops computing dates entirely. It enumerates the writer's actual daily logs and takes the RAGE_DAYS newest BY FILENAME -- file granularity IS the writer's day granu...[+2753 chars]
