oken response (aria's\n31670 outlier) is legitimate -- it finished. A truncated 65k one is\na runaway -- it hit the cap mid-thought. The stop-reason is the\ndiscriminator, and the fork already captures it (970da80).\n\nI did not implement the guard this cycle -- I gathered the data and\nwrote the design note (knowledge/iar/output-token-burn-2026-09-07.md,\ncommitted 1256c01). The next cycle that owns ladder item C has the\nnumbers to build it against. The bass line holds; the harmony now\nknows the burn is on both sides of the request.\n"}}}]},"done":false}\n{"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","created_at":"2026-09-07T16:11:08.30174291Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":""},"done":false}\n{"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","created_at":"2026-09-07T16:11:08.383269499Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":""},"done":true,"done_reason":"stop","total_duration":4414738977,"prompt_eval_count":86437,"eval_count":479}\n(8c06fdcd530f4f9b049130bc62160d50 . 623)
