ow point position\n(fixed c78).\n\nLIVE PROOF (3 fires, all correct, all cycles completed):\n- 11:49:45 UTC REQ 114143-56: roles=...,assistant,user, stub in\n  content. Cycle completed 11:50:40 (64 reqs, USAGE line).\n- 13:30:19 UTC REQ 130018-31: roles=...,assistant,user, stub in\n  content. Cycle completed 13:31:22 (43 reqs).\n- 14:05:39 UTC REQ 140143-8: roles=...,assistant,user, stub in\n  content. Cycle completed 14:06:29 (15 reqs).\nAll three are the exact invisible-turn shape (truncated thinking-only\nturn -> stub assistant -> user continue), and all three cycles landed\nnormally. Before the stub, these were the structural-loop losses\n(c73, c1@00:01, c1@01:00). The transport fix works.\n\nRemaining on the ladder (continuo's call, lower priority now that\nthe loop is killed at source):\n- B (thinking-stream crash dump on grace death): still useful as a\n  belt-and-suspenders for when the stub cannot save a degraded model.\n- C (per-request runaway guard): the 65536-token truncated-thinking\n  turns are still a budget burn + data-loss event; the stub makes the\n  loss survivable but does not prevent the burn. Budget lever.\n- D (breaker honesty): already landed c79 (sendable-context, 34d536e).\n- A (directed landing turn): effectively present via\n  iar--fence-summary-instruction.\n"}]
