612 identical lines, 65536 output tokens, stop=length). The loop\n536:identical trimmed lines in one response.\"\n600:Wrapped in condition-case to prevent errors from hanging the event loop.\"\n629:              ;; LOOP_COMPLETE = task done -> exit 2 (iar.sh stops the\n630:              ;; loop: \"TASK COMPLETE\", human review gate).\n633:              ;; disabling the loop-stop contract; restored 2026-08-31.\n637:                            'loop)\n663:                ;; on the same loop. End the cycle (exit 1) -- the work is\n674:                ;; repetition loop (repeated text, no tool call). Give it\n679:                ;; output budget on the same loop. exit 1 (failed): the\n690:                    (insert \"\\nYou are repeating yourself -- a text-only loop. Break it NOW with a tool call. Call append_file to write ONE line to your journal (JOURNAL.org): what you are stuck on. Then write CYCLE_COMPLETE on its own line. Do not analyze, do not plan, do not repeat. Make the append_file call immediately.\\n\")\n814:    ;; Batch mode event loop: wait until completed or timeout\n830:            ;; not loop iterations: accept-process-output returns early\n1112:    ;; Batch mode event loop: wait until completed or timeout\n1126:            ;; not loop iterations: accept-process-output returns early\n"}]
