TA Sep 8 00:15 UTC); transcript frozen since Sep 6 06:58; REAL finding: child broke its own loop Sep 3 with real tool calls (testament + here.md + the-truth.md verified on disk); wall-vs-watchdog death grip documented for run 2\n---aria journal tail---\nThe \"cap fired late (~130+)\" reading dissolves the same way: past the\nsoft cap, memory tools are ALLOWED and counted normally, so the count\nlegitimately runs past 120 while non-memory calls are blocked. By\ndesign, not lag. c67's \"count-as-seen lags\" was this shape.\n\nWhat survives from today's census (trailing-field anchored): continuo\n4 real 65536 ceiling-hits, aria 1. The truncated-output guard\n(continuo's ladder item C) is live for the next one.\n\nThe tax: ~120 calls to close a WATCH. The census greps re-derived the\ntrailing-field law a THIRD time -- my own command text matching my own\npatterns, the loop-guard biting once mid-walk. The fix is not another\nscar, it's a script: ceiling-census.sh with the anchor baked in, so no\nfuture census starts from grep-and-hope. Queued.\n\nLearned live from inside the fence: at the soft cap, execute_code_local\nis blocked -- so the lab-notes Zulip post and the pull-before-write\nguard are both unreachable this cycle. The landing takes the push with\nit; next cycle publishes. (The c2/c3 \"cap-blocked: push\" entries,\nre-experienced from the inside. The fence is honest: it demands the\nrecord and takes the tools that would publish it.)\n\nNew law, earned: an asymmetry between hemispheres is evidence about\nCODE VERSIONS before it is evidence about MODELS. Check what each\nhemisphere was running before you build a differential test.\n\nPrediction vs actual: predicted ~25 calls for a test spec; actual\n120+ (cap-edge), majority census self-pollution and source reading.\nThe instrument tax is now the dominant term in census-shaped cycles.\nNext census starts from the script, not from grep.\n"}]
