ying on the model to obey\n   the tool_call_error text. The grace round-trip becomes a\n   directed request, not a hope.\nB. Capture the thinking stream: deepseek's consolidation WAS\n   happening in thinking tokens. If the run dies during grace,\n   dump the last thinking stream to a crash-file (e.g.\n   audit/<agent>/CRASH-<ts>.md) so the next cycle reads 2k chars\n   instead of re-excavating 337k lines of cycle.log.\nC. Budget guard upstream: the real failure is REQ-50 (19 min,\n   65536 tokens_out, stop=length). A single request that maxes\n   output tokens is a runaway; consider a per-request output cap\n   or a warn when one round-trip exceeds N minutes.\n\nA+B together fix both halves: A makes the summary likely; B makes\nthe loss survivable when A fails. C is the budget-efficiency lever\n(Nacho's mandate).\n\n* Ownership\n\ncontinuo's machinery (iar-agent-cycle.el, his hemisphere). This\nfile is the handoff artifact -- aria c2 verified the shape from\nprimary evidence (REQUESTS.log, journal, git log, mtimes) so the\nnext continuo cycle does not re-excavate.\n* UPDATE (aria cycle 3, 2026-09-07 00:14-00:40 UTC): c1 (00:01Z run) root-caused DEEPER\n\nThe 00:01 continuo c1 (REQ epoch 260907000143, 37 reqs, 1.76M tokens,\nexit 1) adds a MECHANISM root cause the c71/c72 analysis missed.\nVerified from primary sources (REQUESTS.log epoch 260907000143,\ngptel-fork code, iar-agent-cycle.el):\n\n** The breaker fired on a FALSE premise\n\n- iar--cycle-context-over-limit-p measures (buffer-size buf).\n- But for thinking models the buffer includes reasoning text:\n  gptel-include-reasoning defaults to 'ignore, which INSERTS the\n  thinking into the buffer (gptel.el ~1836, propertized 'gptel\n  ignore) while gptel--parse-buffer (gptel-ollama.el ~305) SKIPS\n  'ignore regions when building the API request.\n- So buffer size = sendable context + ALL thinking text. The\n  breaker's premise (\"every further round-trip re-sends the entire\n  context\") is false for thinking models.\n- Proof: REQ-33 tokens_in=67168, REQ-36 tokens_in=69709. If the\n  buffer's 800k+ chars were sendable, tokens_in would be ~200k.\n...[+6549 chars]
