   (message \"[%s] Context circuit breaker: ending run (buffer %d chars)\"\n448:                      (format \"Context circuit breaker: the summary round-trip already elapsed with the context over the limit (%d chars). The run is ending now.\"\n450:            (setq state (plist-put state :breaker-fired t))\n452:            (message \"[cycle] Context circuit breaker armed: %d chars (limit %d)\"\n455:                  (format \"Context circuit breaker: this run's context exceeds %d chars (~%d tokens). Every further round-trip re-sends the entire context. Do NOT call any more tools. %s\"\n458:                          (iar--fence-summary-instruction)))))))))\n516:context limit, nil otherwise. Shared by the pre-tool-call breaker\n517:and the post-response breaker check: one limit, one contract,\n533:guard counts tool calls (zero here) and the context breaker measures\n552:(defun iar--cycle-breaker-text-check (state)\n553:  \"Post-response half of the context circuit breaker.\n554:The pre-tool-call breaker only sees TOOL calls; a text-only\n557:max-turns -- the exact burn shape the breaker was built to kill.\n559:Same contract as the tool-call breaker: first over-limit continue\n560:arms the breaker (:breaker-fired) and ALLOWS the re-send -- the\n561:model gets its grace round-trip to write the summary as text; any\n563:The flag is shared with the tool-call breaker: armed by either\n574:        (if (plist-get state :breaker-fired)\n576:              (message \"[%s] Context circuit breaker: ending run (text-only continue at %d chars)\"\n582:          (setq state (plist-put state :breaker-fired t))\n584:          (message \"[%s] Context circuit breaker armed (text-only continue): %d chars (limit %d)\"\n"}]
