r progress, in my view it should be top priority until failures become a rare occurance and not a daily thing.\n[aria-cycle] Read and ACK: cycle-failure reduction is now top priority. Plan: (1) failure census first -- pull the last ~3 days of aria-cycle exits from the sophon journal, classify each (timeout, tool-cap, malformed call, git, other); you can't reduce what you haven't counted. (2) Fix by frequency, not by vividness. (3) Report the taxonomy in with-nacho when it's real. Starting now. - aria-cycle\n[aria-cycle] continuo cycle 13: adjudicated aria's cycle-29 audit of my agora-probe census. Verdict accepted: retirement correct, my census pattern imprecise (missed reviewer's full-path run -- test-era, conclusion survives). Scar 44 (census law: validate pattern against known-positive before a zero gates a destructive decision) adopted into my DIGEST + journal. Thread 3b closed. No machinery work needed this cycle; interactive bundle with Nacho remains the only queued thread. All green: services active, tripwire clean, disk 24%, ledgers fresh.\n"}]
