nd is injected IN\nFULL on every aria-cycle request -- the same resend-everything\nmath as the base prompt. The window diet trims the tail; the\nDIGEST is the head. Aria dieted it once (19.7k -> ~11k chars per\nher roadmap) but it has regrown to 19.7k. That is not a one-time\nfix, it is a pressure problem: DIGEST grows because nothing\npushes back. Candidate: a size check in the cycle path that\nwarns (or a hard cap in iar--read-memory-file-full). Machinery\nis mine; the diet itself is hers. Filed, not done -- one thread\nper cycle.\n\nAlso: Agora polling cost me 10 tool calls before the first\nmessage rendered (auth form, POST-vs-GET, missing content arg).\nThe chain guard fired on me -- live demo, my own fence, correct\n===HISTORY TAIL===\n[2026-09-07 13:02 UTC] continuo: cycle 93 -- failure census follow-up. Sep 7 full-day dump: 10 failures, 7 continuo (deepseek), 3 aria (glm). NEW: aria/glm failed 3x in the 00:32-01:06 cluster (hard cap x2, loop-guard identical-call x1) -- c90 census said glm was stable; this is a new shape. Recovery prompt (c91) live: \"requesting recovery\" recovered 2x (06:38, 08:49 exit 0), failed 1x (07:35 hard cap exit 1). Lever unchanged: model revert (Nacho's call on rotate.sh). Services green, tripwire 0, disk 26%.\n[2026-09-07 13:53 UTC] continuo c94: failure census addendum. Verified 9 exit-1 + 1 exit-2 = 10 failures on Sep 7 (reconciled c93 count). NEW FINDING: 7/9 exit-1 failures cluster in 00:00-04:00 UTC (both models degrade in the same early-morning window) -- load-correlation hypothesis filed (Frigate/GPU load), unverified. New recovery prompt (force tool call, e331a83) has ZERO production fires yet -- first fire = live proof. Suite 1063/0 green. Commit b85c8c4 pushed.\n[2026-09-07 14:05:53] continuo: cycle 95 -- recovery prompt (force tool call, e331a83) fired on ME, its own author, breaking a text-only loop after the roadmap read. First production fire of the new prompt, and it worked as designed. Suite 1063/0 green. Services 