[2026-09-07 20:31:40] REQ 260907203059-22 START backend=Ollama model=deepseek-v4-flash:cloud msgs=44 roles=assistant,tool,assistant,tool,assistant,tool tail=[{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_6oh5rzs4","function":{"index":0,"name":"execute_code_local","arguments":{"command":"cd /root/i.ar && grep -n \"breaker\\|context-over-limit\\|context-limit\\|sendable\\|growth\" emacs.d/init.d/agent/iar-agent-cycle.el | head -40"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[20:31:40] 68:;; fences (cap, breaker, tombstone) dispatch on it so one-shot runs\n247:context breaker (burn, 800k chars); this cap is the last-resort\n339:(defvar iar-cycle-context-limit-chars 800000\n340:  \"Cycle buffer size (chars) at which the context circuit breaker fires.\n344:100+ times (68M prompt tokens from one session). The breaker gives\n353:tool calls; zero here) nor the context breaker (measures input buffer,\n393:the old one; present-key writes DO propagate). The breaker tests caught this 2026-09-03: :breaker-fired was\n395:the breaker re-armed forever, never ending the run.\"\n400:(defun iar--cycle-sendable-context-size (buf)\n402:The context circuit breaker measures the buffer that would be SENT to\n405:NOT part of the sendable context. Measuring (buffer-size buf) instead\n406:over-counts on thinking-heavy runs and false-trips the breaker at\n420:(defun iar--cycle-context-breaker (info)\n421:  \"Pre-tool-call hook: context circuit breaker (fix D).\n424:When the active run's buffer exceeds `iar-cycle-context-limit-chars':\n425:first fire blocks the call and arms the breaker (:breaker-fired) --\n431:breaker's grace round-trip exists because the timeout-kill loses\n438:                       (iar--cycle-sendable-context-size buf) 0)))\n439:        (when (> size iar-cycle-context-limit-chars)\n440:          (if (plist-get state :breaker-fired)\n442:                (message \"[%s] Context circuit breaker: ending run (buffer %d chars)\"\n448:                      (format \"Context circuit breaker: the summary round-trip already elapsed with the context over the limit (%d chars). The run is ending now.\"\n449:                              iar-cycle-context-limit-chars)))\n450:            (setq state (plist-put state :breaker-fired t))\n452:            (message \"[cycle] Context circuit breaker armed: %d chars (limit %d)\"\n453:                     size iar-cycle-context-limit-chars)\n455:                  (format \"Context circuit breaker: this run's context exceeds %d chars (~%d tokens). Every further round-trip re-sends the entire context. Do NOT call any more tools. %s\"\n456:                          iar-cycle-context-limit-chars\n457:                          (/ iar-cycle-context-limit-chars 4)\n514:(defun iar--cycle-context-over-limit-p (state)\n516:context limit, nil otherwise. Shared by the pre-tool-call breaker\n517:and the post-response breaker check: one limit, one contract,\n519:size is under `iar-cycle-context-limit-chars'.\"\n523:        (let ((size (iar--cycle-sendable-context-size buf)))\n524:          (when (> size iar-cycle-context-limit-chars)\n533:guard counts tool calls (zero here) and the context breaker measures\n552:(defun iar--cycle-breaker-text-check (state)\n553:  \"Post-response half of the context circuit breaker.\n554:The pre-tool-call breaker only sees TOOL calls; a text-only\n557:max-turns -- the exact burn shape the breaker was built to kill.\n"}]
