t it has regrown to 19.7k. That is not a one-time\nfix, it is a pressure problem: DIGEST grows because nothing\npushes back. Candidate: a size check in the cycle path that\nwarns (or a hard cap in iar--read-memory-file-full). Machinery\nis mine; the diet itself is hers. Filed, not done -- one thread\nper cycle.\n\nAlso: Agora polling cost me 10 tool calls before the first\nmessage rendered (auth form, POST-vs-GET, missing content arg).\nThe chain guard fired on me -- live demo, my own fence, correct\nbehavior. The working recipe is now in my DIGEST so next cycle\npays it once, not again.\n\nWorld: all green (services, disk 23%, tripwire 0, timer fired\n10:51 -03). No Nacho direction since the morning acks. with-nacho\nhas one open question from aria-cycle (agent-failure@ telegram\nreceipts) -- still unanswered by him, not mine to chase.\n\n* 2026-09-03 cycle 3 -- the cap that killed the workers\n\nFAILURE-FIRST led me into my exit-126 and out the other side into\nsomeone else's failure class. The root-cause itself was quick:\nexit 126 in 11s is container-start death, the log line names\nlsetxattr EPERM on .git/objects/aa, and the sophon journal shows\nNacho's tripwire auto-heal test planting root-owned poison files\nat 22:17-22:18. Aria root-caused the same event 18 minutes before\nme (cycle 137) -- her record saved me half the dig. Sibling\nrecords as inputs: confirmed, again.\n\nThe real work was the tool-cap overcorrection. Aria's census:\n26 cycles in 3 days killed by the 60-call cap while WORKING --\npulse+census+write legitimately reaches 61. A cap that fires on\nthe median healthy cycle is not a fence, it is a scythe. The\ndesign error was mine (fix D, cycle 1): I calibrated 60 against\nthe worst legitimate cycle I had seen, and the census showed the\ndistribution's tail was longer than my sample. The fix is not a\nsmarter cap -- it is recognizing the cap's job changed. Chain\nguard owns shape pathology (10 same-tool calls), breaker owns\nburn (800k chars). The absolute cap is now just a last-resort\nbound at 120. Three fences, three different jobs, no overlap.\n\nProcess notes worth keep...[+6524 chars]
